1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:00,980
Welcome back!

2
00:00:01,940 --> 00:00:04,620
Last time we learned about two pairs of

3
00:00:04,620 --> 00:00:06,920
letters that come at the end of words.

4
00:00:08,160 --> 00:00:11,720
We learn that NG makes one sound together

5
00:00:13,280 --> 00:00:18,340
and NK makes that same sound with a K sound at the end.

6
00:00:19,820 --> 00:00:22,160
You listened really carefully and

7
00:00:22,160 --> 00:00:24,660
today we're going to finish level five.

8
00:00:25,860 --> 00:00:27,740
We have two more things to learn.

9
00:00:28,840 --> 00:00:28,940
First,

10
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:33,660
we'll meet the letter X which is a very unusual letter.

11
00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:38,500
Then we'll meet the letter W which likes to play tricks.

12
00:00:39,920 --> 00:00:40,580
Let's start!

13
00:00:42,340 --> 00:00:45,600
I want to show you something surprising about the letter X.

14
00:00:47,180 --> 00:00:50,340
Every other letter you know makes one sound.

15
00:00:51,580 --> 00:00:53,280
But the letter X is different.

16
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:58,240
The letter X makes two sounds all by itself.

17
00:00:59,740 --> 00:01:00,840
Listen to this word,

18
00:01:01,660 --> 00:01:03,740
FOX. Say it with me,

19
00:01:04,760 --> 00:01:04,980
FOX.

20
00:01:06,740 --> 00:01:08,580
Now listen right at the end,

21
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:10,060
FOX.

22
00:01:11,840 --> 00:01:12,560
Can you hear it?

23
00:01:13,700 --> 00:01:15,880
There are two sounds hiding in there.

24
00:01:16,980 --> 00:01:17,320
First,

25
00:01:18,300 --> 00:01:18,380
K,

26
00:01:19,880 --> 00:01:20,380
then S.

27
00:01:22,840 --> 00:01:23,460
Say them with me,

28
00:01:24,140 --> 00:01:26,150
K, S.

29
00:01:27,900 --> 00:01:28,820
Now say them quickly,

30
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:30,400
K, S.

31
00:01:31,940 --> 00:01:33,940
That's the sound the letter X makes.

32
00:01:35,120 --> 00:01:38,240
One letter but two sounds join together.

33
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:41,660
Let's read some X words.

34
00:01:42,900 --> 00:01:46,260
FOX. The fox has a bushy tail.

35
00:01:48,140 --> 00:01:50,900
BOX. We put the toys in the box.

36
00:01:52,920 --> 00:01:55,240
SIX. I can count to six.

37
00:01:57,240 --> 00:02:00,400
MIX. We mix the flour and the eggs.

38
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:04,960
FIX. Dad will fix my bike.

39
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:09,320
Wax. The candle is made of wax.

40
00:02:11,340 --> 00:02:12,740
Look at all those words.

41
00:02:13,720 --> 00:02:15,860
Everyone ends with the letter X.

42
00:02:16,660 --> 00:02:21,360
And every time that one letter is doing the work of two sounds.

43
00:02:22,820 --> 00:02:22,920
FOX.

44
00:02:24,640 --> 00:02:24,860
BOX.

45
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:26,760
SIX.

46
00:02:28,280 --> 00:02:30,240
You're reading those really well.

47
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:34,080
Here's something important to remember.

48
00:02:35,100 --> 00:02:36,940
Do you remember the floss rule?

49
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:40,640
We double F, L,

50
00:02:41,260 --> 00:02:42,180
S and Z.

51
00:02:43,720 --> 00:02:44,680
But we never,

52
00:02:45,320 --> 00:02:49,440
ever double X. There's no word like FOX.

53
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:53,520
ONE X is always enough.

54
00:02:55,080 --> 00:02:58,280
So if you hear the X sound at the end of a word,

55
00:02:58,960 --> 00:03:00,000
write ONE X,

56
00:03:00,540 --> 00:03:01,400
never two.

57
00:03:03,340 --> 00:03:06,300
Now let's meet our last letter of level five.

58
00:03:06,940 --> 00:03:08,580
The tricky letter W.

59
00:03:09,780 --> 00:03:12,840
The letter W likes to change things.

60
00:03:13,680 --> 00:03:14,540
Let me show you.

61
00:03:16,280 --> 00:03:18,920
Normally the letter A says air.

62
00:03:20,060 --> 00:03:21,910
You can hear it in cat,

63
00:03:23,080 --> 00:03:23,760
cat.

64
00:03:25,300 --> 00:03:28,000
But watch what happens when W comes first.

65
00:03:29,660 --> 00:03:31,860
WANT. Say it with me.

66
00:03:33,160 --> 00:03:33,580
WANT.

67
00:03:35,360 --> 00:03:36,220
Did you hear that?

68
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:39,820
The A didn't say air this time.

69
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:41,310
It said O.

70
00:03:42,700 --> 00:03:45,860
WANT. The W changed it.

71
00:03:47,500 --> 00:03:48,960
Listen to some more words.

72
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:52,820
WASH. We wash our hands.

73
00:03:54,620 --> 00:03:56,960
WATCH. I watch the birds.

74
00:03:58,820 --> 00:04:01,960
SWAN. The swan swims on the lake.

75
00:04:03,820 --> 00:04:06,580
WAND. The fairy waves her wand.

76
00:04:08,220 --> 00:04:09,080
Listen to the vowel.

77
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:10,560
WANT.

78
00:04:12,160 --> 00:04:19,040
WASH. WATCH. SWAN. It says O every time.

79
00:04:20,200 --> 00:04:22,360
Even though we write the letter A.

80
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:25,900
That's the trick W likes to play.

81
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:28,900
But here's something important.

82
00:04:30,100 --> 00:04:32,680
W doesn't do this in every word.

83
00:04:34,020 --> 00:04:39,340
LISTEN. WAG. The dog can wag his tail.

84
00:04:41,040 --> 00:04:43,700
Here the A still says air.

85
00:04:44,630 --> 00:04:49,280
WAG. So this isn't a rule that works every time.

86
00:04:50,200 --> 00:04:50,650
It's a small

87
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:53,240
family of words you learn by sight.

88
00:04:54,960 --> 00:04:56,460
Here's what good readers do.

89
00:04:57,620 --> 00:04:59,180
When you see W with A,

90
00:05:00,180 --> 00:05:02,320
try the O sound first.

91
00:05:03,460 --> 00:05:04,580
Then ask yourself,

92
00:05:05,240 --> 00:05:06,640
is that a real word?

93
00:05:07,900 --> 00:05:09,280
If it is, great.

94
00:05:10,640 --> 00:05:13,260
If it isn't, try air instead.

95
00:05:14,580 --> 00:05:15,660
That's exactly how

96
00:05:15,680 --> 00:05:17,040
good readers read.

97
00:05:18,860 --> 00:05:21,180
Let's remember all six rules.

98
00:05:22,340 --> 00:05:24,680
Rule 1. The floss rule.

99
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:29,700
Rule 2. C, K and C, K.

100
00:05:30,150 --> 00:05:37,600
Rule 3. NG. Rule 4. NK.

101
00:05:39,340 --> 00:05:43,200
Rule 5. The letter X makes two sounds.

102
00:05:44,540 --> 00:05:49,660
And rule 6. The tricky letter W can change A to

103
00:05:49,660 --> 00:05:51,020
the O sound.

104
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:53,120
Fantastic.

105
00:05:54,080 --> 00:05:58,680
You've learned all six spelling rules in level 5. I'm really

106
00:05:59,020 --> 00:05:59,720
proud of you.

107
00:06:01,020 --> 00:06:05,420
Level 5 is one of the hardest levels and you finished it.

108
00:06:06,580 --> 00:06:07,700
Next time, we'll

109
00:06:07,700 --> 00:06:11,820
start level 6 together and learn some brand new sounds.

110
00:06:12,540 --> 00:06:13,300
Don't miss it.

111
00:06:14,840 --> 00:06:15,840
If you enjoyed this

112
00:06:15,940 --> 00:06:16,320
lesson,

113
00:06:16,880 --> 00:06:19,040
please like this video and subscribe.

114
00:06:20,180 --> 00:06:22,700
And practice all six rules in the English

115
00:06:22,840 --> 00:06:23,620
learning app.

116
00:06:24,360 --> 00:06:27,540
It's free on the Apple App Store and Google Play.

117
00:06:28,700 --> 00:06:28,820
